# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — Physical state contract for chronicles-of-slavia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements.
# Run with: must check
# Fix with: must fix (where a deterministic fix exists)
#
# CORRECTED 2026-07-17. This file previously declared itself the contract for
# `rsr-template-repo` — inherited verbatim from the template this repo was
# instantiated from. Four of its sixteen probes failed when actually run, two of
# them because they were unpassable by construction rather than merely stale:
#
#   * contractiles-files-present — checked the pre-trident flat paths
#     (contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml) that INDEX.a2ml v2.0.0 moved into per-verb
#     directories (contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml) on 2026-04-18.
#   * self-validating-structure  — required a k9-svc/ directory that has never
#     existed here; the three k9 tier templates live in self-validating/.
#   * no-placeholder-values      — grepped for `{{` across contractiles/ and so
#     matched its own `- run:` line. Unpassable in ANY repo, including the
#     template. See the Identity section for why it is gone rather than fixed.
#   * template-readonly          — grepped for an RSR_TEMPLATE_DO_NOT_EDIT
#     marker present nowhere in this repo except inside the probe looking for
#     it. It also asserts template integrity, which is rsr-template-repo's
#     business, not an instantiated game's.
#
# NOTE (2026-07-17): nothing executes this file. There is no `must` binary in
# this repo or on PATH, and the coaptation receipt records all sixteen probes as
# `probe-deferred` — deferred to a Hunt-tier runner that does not exist yet
# (estate-wide; the runners are unbuilt). Until one lands, these probes are
# claims, not gates. They are written to be run, and were each run by hand on
# 2026-07-17, but do not mistake this file for enforcement.

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for chronicles-of-slavia — a two-character Slavic-
folkloric narrative game, instantiated from rsr-template-repo but NOT that
template (see ECOSYSTEM.a2ml `what-this-is-not`). These are hard requirements:
a single failure is intended to block release once a runner exists.
@end

## File Presence

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist
- run: test -f LICENSE
- severity: critical

### readme-present
- description: README.adoc must exist
- run: test -f README.adoc
- severity: critical

### security-policy
- description: SECURITY.md must exist
- run: test -f SECURITY.md || test -f .github/SECURITY.md
- severity: critical

### ai-manifest
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml must exist
- run: test -f 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical

### governance-docs
- description: GOVERNANCE.adoc, MAINTAINERS.adoc, CODEOWNERS must exist
- run: test -f GOVERNANCE.adoc && test -f MAINTAINERS.adoc && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable
- severity: critical

## Directory Structure

### contractiles-complete
- description: All required contractile directories exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable/contractiles && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/bust && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/dust
- severity: critical

### contractiles-files-present
- description: All four primary contractile files exist, on the trident shape
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/intend/Intentfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/trust/Trustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/adjust/Adjustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical
- notes: Paths follow INDEX.a2ml v2.0.0 (2026-04-18), which moved every verb into its own directory. The flat contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml layout this probe used to assert has not existed since.

### bust-dust-files-present
- description: Bustfile and Dustfile exist in their directories
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### six-directory-present
- description: descriptiles directory exists with required files
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/META.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/PLAYBOOK.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/AGENTIC.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/NEUROSYM.a2ml
- severity: critical

### anchors-directory
- description: anchors directory exists in descriptiles
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles/anchors
- severity: warning

### self-validating-structure
- description: self-validating directory has the three k9 tier templates and examples
- run: test -d .machine_readable/self-validating && test -d .machine_readable/self-validating/examples && test -f .machine_readable/self-validating/template-kennel.k9.ncl && test -f .machine_readable/self-validating/template-yard.k9.ncl && test -f .machine_readable/self-validating/template-hunt.k9.ncl
- severity: warning
- notes: Asserts the Kennel/Yard/Hunt tiers by name rather than a k9-svc/ directory, which has never existed here. INDEX.a2ml still lists the k9 templates under contractiles/k9/ — also wrong; they live in self-validating/. Reported upstream, not patched here.

## Identity

# Replaces the old `no-placeholder-values` and `template-readonly` probes.
#
# `no-placeholder-values` grepped for `{{` and is not merely stale but
# unfixable as posed: a regex cannot tell a placeholder from the word
# "placeholder". STATE.a2ml and ANCHOR.a2ml both legitimately DOCUMENT the
# residue problem, and every mention trips the detector — as does the probe's
# own source line. Any repo honest enough to write down that it has placeholder
# residue would fail a check for placeholder residue.
#
# Placeholder residue is real (STATE.a2ml puts it at ~150 files) but it is
# `dust`'s remit, not `must`'s: dust.no-example-placeholders and
# dust.no-stale-template-references already track it as planned exnovation,
# where an advisory grade fits work that is expected to take time. A blocking
# must-probe duplicating them bought nothing.
#
# What `must` can assert precisely is the invariant whose breach was the actual
# bug: that this repo declares its own identity. Anchored to the value lines, so
# the historical notes in CLADE's header do not match.

### identity-substituted
- description: CLADE declares this repo's own derived identity, not the template's
- run: test "$(grep -E '^uuid = ' .machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml)" = 'uuid = "b1507e91-78ca-5d30-a66c-dc675ad678f0"' && test "$(grep -E '^canonical-name = ' .machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml)" = 'canonical-name = "chronicles-of-slavia"'
- severity: critical
- notes: Until 2026-07-16 this repo declared uuid a5ea1382-a34c-5334-8a46-a2ebe904c810 / rsr-template-repo — the template's own genuine identity — so it told every arriving agent it was the template. The uuid is UUIDv5(URL, "github.com/hyperpolymath/chronicles-of-slavia"); see CLADE.a2ml for the derivation. Verified to fail when canonical-name is reverted.

## Golden Path

### golden-path-executes
- description: `just test` runs the real suite rather than echoing success
- run: grep -q 'cargo test -p slavia-core' Justfile
- severity: critical
- notes: Guards the fix in PR #7. Until 2026-07-17 the test/lint/fmt/fmt-check recipes were stubs that printed "Tests passed!" and ran nothing, so `just quality` was three no-ops reporting success while ANCHOR.a2ml declared that same path verifies Zone A's five beats, the ESM testbed and L2 determinism. A grep is a weak assertion — it catches reversion to a stub, not a suite that has rotted — but it is honest about what it checks, which the recipe it guards was not.

## Git State

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: All contractile files are tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/ 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### signed-commits
- description: All commits must be signed
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: critical
